From: LGA1150 <9155358+LGA1150@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tls: add an aligned out-of-place RX experiment

Keep the cloned, potentially fragmented ciphertext as the AEAD input,
while aligning the private plaintext payload to the DMA cache alignment.
This opt-in comparison uses rx_inplace=0 rx_aligned_output=1 and avoids
the private ciphertext copy. It allows DMA-backed AEADs to write directly
to the plaintext pages if they can handle fragmented input separately.

Default behavior and direct-to-userspace receive are unchanged.

---
--- a/net/tls/tls_sw.c
+++ b/net/tls/tls_sw.c
@@ -56,6 +56,10 @@
 module_param(rx_inplace, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(rx_inplace, "Decrypt buffered async RX records in private aligned buffers");
 
+static bool rx_aligned_output;
+module_param(rx_aligned_output, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(rx_aligned_output, "Align buffered async RX output without copying ciphertext (rx_inplace=0)");
+
 struct tls_rx_record {
 	struct list_head list;
 	struct sk_buff *skb;
@@ -1694,7 +1698,7 @@
 		/* Align the payload, leaving the record header immediately before
 		 * it. Subsequent fragments start at page boundaries.
 		 */
-		if (inplace)
+		if (inplace || (ctx->async_capable && READ_ONCE(rx_aligned_output)))
 			headroom = ALIGN(prot->prepend_size,
 					 dma_get_cache_alignment()) - prot->prepend_size;
 
